On Saturday morning the café is full.
I am working together with Elif again today.
We have a lot of customers today.
The work is routine for me now.
A man comes to the counter.
"Good morning, what can I get you?" I ask him.
"I would like a large coffee and two Brötchen," he says.
"Gladly, that will be six euros fifty," I answer.
He pays and I give him the coffee.
Elif is standing at the other till.
"Maya, can you please pack up three chocolate Brötchen?" she asks me.
"Sure, I will do it right away," I say.
I pack the Brötchen into a small paper bag.
Everything goes so fast and easily today.
I do not even have to think about the individual steps anymore.
A woman orders a piece of cake to go.
"Do you need the receipt?" I ask her politely.
"No, thank you," she says, smiling.
The Saturday morning in the café just flies by.
